          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Given some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"}> site
            )
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of test spaces, suppose one fixes some category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Corr
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Corr_p(S)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            equipped with certain cohomological data on their correspondence space. Then a
            %em sheaf with transfer
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a contravariant functor on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Corr
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Corr_p(S)
            such that the restriction along the canonical embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Corr
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \to Corr_p(S)
            makes the resulting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
          %p
            Traditionally this is considered for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nisnevich+site"} Nisnevich site
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Corr
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Corr_p(S)
            constructed from correspondences equipped with algebraic cycles as discussed at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+motive"} pure motive
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Voevodsky00"} Voevodsky 00, 2.1 and def. 3.1.1
          %p
            The idea is that, looking at it the other way around, the extension of a sheaf to a sheaf with transfer defines a kind of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Umkehr+map"} Umkehr map
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} fiber integration
            by which the sheaf is not only pulled back along maps, but also pushed forward, hence “transferred” (this concept of course makes sense rather generally in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Piacenza84"} Piacenza 84, 1.1
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+categories"} derived categories
            of those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaves"} abelian sheaves
            with transfers for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nisnevich+site"} Nisnevich site
            with are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A1-homotopy+theory"} A1-homotopy invariant
            provides a model for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motive"} motives
            known as
            %em
              %a{:href => "motive#VoevodskyMotives"} Voevodsky motives
            or similar (
            %a{:href => "#Voevodsky00"}> Voevodsky 00, p. 20
            ).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            On this page we construct the category of Nisnevich sheaves with transfer over a base scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            which is assumed to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+scheme"} regular
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noetherian+scheme"} noetherian
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Deglise"} Déglise
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mixed+motives"} mixed motives
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                be a base
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
                which is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+scheme"} regular
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noetherian+scheme"} noetherian
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sm
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sm_S
                denote the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
                that are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth"} smooth
                and of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
                over
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sm
                          %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in \Sm_S
                %strong
                  finite
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_S(X, Y)
                as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
                generated by closed integral subschemes
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi S
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \subset X \times_S Y
                such that the projection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \to X
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite"} finite
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    equidimensional
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/equidimensional+morphism"} ?
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Sm
                        %mi S
                        %mi cor
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sm_S^{cor}
                whose objects are the same as
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sm
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sm_S
                and whose morphisms are finite
                = succeed "-correspondences." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %li
              %p
                Note that there is a canonical functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mi S
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sm
                        %mi S
                      %mo →
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sm
                        %mi S
                        %mi cor
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_S : \Sm_S \to \Sm_S^cor
                which acts on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                by taking the finite correspondence induced by its
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
            %li
              %p
                Recall that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibred+product"} fibred product
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                defines a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+structure"} symmetric monoidal structure
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sm
                          %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sm_S
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+structure"} symmetric monoidal structure
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sm
                          %mi S
                          %mi cor
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sm_S^{cor}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_S
                respects these structures.
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_S
                (resp.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi P
                          %mi S
                          %mi tr
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_S^{tr}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+presheaves"} abelian presheaves
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sm
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sm_S
                (resp. on
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sm
                          %mi S
                          %mi cor
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sm_S^{cor}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi P
                        %mi S
                        %mi tr
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_S^{tr}
                are called
                %strong presheaves with transfer
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S[X]
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
                with transfers
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable"} represented
                by an object
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sm
                          %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \Sm_S
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_S
                denote the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sm
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sm_S
                with respect to the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nisnevich+topology"} Nisnevich topology
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi N
                        %mi S
                        %mi tr
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msubsup
                        %mi P
                        %mi S
                        %mi tr
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_S^{tr} \subset P_S^{tr}
                be the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                spanned by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sm
                        %mi S
                        %mi cor
                      %mo →
                      %mi Ab
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : \Sm_S^{cor} \to Ab
                whose
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mi S
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sm
                        %mi S
                      %mo →
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sm
                        %mi S
                        %mi cor
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_S : \Sm_S \to \Sm_S^{cor}
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sm
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sm_S
                (with respect to the
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nisnevich+topology"} Nisnevich topology
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi N
                        %mi S
                        %mi tr
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_S^{tr}
                are called
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong Nisnevich sheaves with transfer
            %li
              %p
                %strong Proposition.
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi N
                        %mi S
                        %mi tr
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_S^{tr}
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete"} cocomplete
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+abelian+category"} Grothendieck abelian
                with an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+small"} essentially small
                set of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators"} generators
                given by the objects
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S[X]
                for
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sm
                          %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \Sm_S
            %li
              %p
                This allows one to define a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+structure"} symmetric monoidal structure
                on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi N
                          %mi S
                          %mi tr
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_S^{tr}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sm
                        %mi S
                      %mo →
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} N
                        %mi S
                        %mi tr
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sm_S \to \N_S^{tr}
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal"} symmetric monoidal
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msubsup
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi S
                        %mi tr
                      %mo −
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - \otimes_S^{tr} -
                preserves
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi N
                          %mi S
                          %mi tr
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_S^{tr}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} colim
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo →
                          %mi F
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ;
                      %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                      %mi G
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} colim
                        %mrow
                          %mi Y
                          %mo →
                          %mi G
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F = \colim_{X \to F} L_S[X] ; \qquad G = \colim_{Y \to G} L_S[Y]
              %p
                where the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
                are taken over the family of morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S[X] \to F
                (resp.
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S[Y] \to G
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %msubsup
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi S
                        %mi tr
                      %mi G
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} colim
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo →
                          %mi F
                          %mo ;
                          %mi Y
                          %mo →
                          %mi G
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi S
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \otimes_S^{tr} G = \colim_{X \to F ; Y \to G} L_S[X \times_S Y].
            %li
              %p
                This
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+structure"} symmetric monoidal structure
                is further
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+structure"} closed
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Hom
                          %mo ̲
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi N
                            %mi S
                            %mi tr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Hom
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi N
                            %mi S
                            %mi tr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %msubsup
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi S
                        %mi tr
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underline{\Hom}_{N_S^{tr}} (F,G) (X) = \Hom_{N_S^{tr}} (F \otimes_S^{tr} L_S[X], G)
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sm
                          %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \Sm_S
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
